<title>GERMANY: German weather ideal for spring plantings.</title>
<headline>German weather ideal for spring plantings.</headline>
<dateline>OFFENBACH 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>German spring plantings will be aided by dry weather after rains in February, the DWD national meteorological office said.</p>
<p>&quot;Precipitation in February made up for lack of rain in December and January,&quot; a farm weather analyst said.</p>
<p>&quot;Soils have become accessible, especially in the north, where spring barley and oats are being sown, while farmers in the south will have to wait a little longer,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>Cooler weather was expected for the weekend but maximum daytime temperatures over the next seven days should be 12 to 15 degrees and night lows only up to a few degrees below zero.</p>
<p>Plantings should continue quickly and without disruption under such conditions.</p>
<p>Winter grain and rapeseed crops were developing well and no further winter damage had been reported after some problems in north-eastern Germany.</p>
<p>--Hamburg newsroom +49-40-41903275</p>
